{
  "0": "Training strategy: replace the learning-rate schedule with cosine decay from the current initial rate to 10% of that rate over 200 epochs. Unlike the unsuccessful constant rate reduction, this retains larger early updates while reducing late oscillation. Preserve optimizer, batch size, dropout, weight decay, architecture and loss. Apply to all four datasets with one model per category and unchanged seeds, routing and validation checkpoint selection.",
  "1": "Learning objective: replace the ranking loss with hard-negative-weighted pairwise logistic loss: sum_j w_j softplus(s_neg_j - s_pos), where w=softmax(stop_gradient(s_neg)) over the existing sampled negatives. This emphasizes ranking mistakes without changing sampling or adding a predictor. Preserve features, GRU, scoring and all training settings. Train one model per category across all four datasets with unchanged seeds and routing.",
  "2": "Network architecture: add layer normalization to the reset-gate, update-gate and candidate preactivations inside each existing GRU cell, preserving its reset convention, hidden width and layer count. More stable gate scales may improve recurrent optimization without increasing recurrent depth or history length. Preserve embeddings, features, readout, scoring, loss and optimizer. Apply to all four datasets; update the predictor writer to load the same architecture and one checkpoint per category.",
  "3": "Interaction mechanism: replace dot-product compatibility with diagonal bilinear scoring s(h,i)=sum_k d_k h_k e_i,k, initializing the jointly trained vector d to ones. This starts at the existing dot product and can learn which recurrent dimensions best discriminate candidates with only linear parameter overhead. Preserve GRU topology, embeddings, history readout, loss and optimizer. Apply to all four datasets and update the predictor writer; load one model per category."
}
